# Normalise text to LF in the repository.
#
# Two things depend on this:
#   1. build_docs.sh runs on an Ubuntu CI runner. With CRLF endings the shebang
#      becomes "/usr/bin/env bash\r" and the job fails with a bad-interpreter
#      error that is famously confusing to diagnose.
#   2. CI regenerates docs/ and fails if the result differs from what is
#      committed. If HTML were committed with CRLF from Windows and regenerated
#      with LF on Linux, every file would differ and the check would be useless.
#
# Working copies still get native endings on checkout; this governs what is
# stored.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF even on a Windows checkout - Git Bash runs them.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Stata reads either, but keep them consistent with everything else.
*.do   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.csv  text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.cff  text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf

# Binary - never touch these.
*.dta  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.png  binary
*.pdf  binary

# Keep generated docs out of diffs and language statistics: they are build
# output, and a one-line source edit can rewrite a whole embedded-resource file.
docs/*.html linguist-generated=true -diff
